  <docvars>
    <docvar key="instr-class" value="sve"/>
    <docvar key="isa" value="A64"/>
  </docvars>
  <heading>ZIP1, ZIP2 (vectors)</heading>
  <desc>
    <brief>
      <para>Interleave elements from two half vectors</para>
    </brief>
    <authored>
      <para>This instruction interleaves alternating  elements
from the lowest or highest halves of the
first and second source vectors, and places the values in
the destination vector.  This instruction is unpredicated.</para>
      <para>The High halves (quadwords) and Low halves (quadwords) variants require an Effective SVE vector
length of at least 256 bits.
ID_AA64ZFR0_EL1.F64MM or ID_AA64ZFR0_EL1.EltPerm indicates whether the High halves (quadwords) and Low halves (quadwords) variants
are implemented.
The High halves (quadwords) and Low halves (quadwords) variants
are legal when executed in Streaming SVE mode if FEAT_SVE_PERM256 is implemented.</para>
    </authored>
    <predicated>False</predicated>
    <uses_dit condition="FEAT_SVE2 is implemented or FEAT_SME is implemented">True</uses_dit>
    <sm_policy>SM_0_only</sm_policy>
  </desc>
  <operationalnotes>
    <operationalnote>
